// expect-exit: 0
// A POSITION IS A TICK OF THE WALK (DEF-496, RULED 2026-11-03): a macro body's text is where the macro is declared, so the order of the text isn't the order the code runs. Each form twice: `_b` with its macro declared before the function, `_a` after it. On the walk that read spans one of each pair reads wrong, a wrong value or a false trap, and the other reads right by luck of the text.
// Each case takes its value as a parameter, so no optimiser can forward a constant past the park, and returns 7. Each is its own spawned task, as `async_loop_clause_read_ok.npk`'s are, or the children read right under `main`'s frame on the broken walk too. A wrong value is `#unreachable()`, exit 74.
mod:async_macro_walk_order_ok;
